const archiveCollections=[['historical-photographs','Historical Photographs','A photograph can hold a face, a place, and a day that no written record kept. This collection is for images whose source, date, and permission are known.','Photographs Waiting for Their Captions'],['documents-and-publications','Documents and Publications','Programmes, newsletters, constitutions, and clippings carry the ordinary paperwork of a community. This collection is for documents that can be described and shared responsibly.','Paper Records and Printed Matter'],['anniversary-records','Anniversary Records','Anniversaries mark the years a community chose to remember. This collection gathers the programmes, souvenirs, and photographs that recorded those occasions.','Marking the Years Together'],['chapter-histories','Chapter Histories','Every chapter has a beginning that only its own members witnessed. This collection is for the written histories, rosters, and recollections that chapters preserved.','How Chapters Told Their Own Story'],['news-coverage','News Coverage','Newspapers and broadcast reports are a record of how the wider public saw the fraternity at a particular moment. This collection keeps that outside view alongside the internal one.','What the Press Recorded'],['videos','Videos','Moving images preserve voice, movement, and gathering in a way that a still photograph cannot. This collection points to video material held on its original public platforms.','Recordings and Moving Images'],['memorabilia','Memorabilia','Shirts, pins, banners, and objects carry memory in a form that documents do not. This collection is for the physical items members kept.','Objects Members Kept'],['certificates','Certificates','Certificates record recognition at a particular time, by a particular body. This collection keeps those documents with their issuing context intact.','Recognition and Its Context'],['posters','Posters','Posters announce something that was about to happen. Read years later, they show what a community thought worth announcing.','Announcements on Paper'],['council-records','Council Records','Councils coordinate work that no single chapter could do alone. This collection is for the records that document that coordination.','Records of Coordinated Work'],['oral-histories','Oral Histories','Some history was never written down. It lives in the memory of members who were there, and it survives only if someone records it. This collection is for those accounts.','Stories Told Out Loud'],['historical-timelines','Historical Timelines','A timeline is an argument about what mattered and in what order. This collection gathers the chronological records different communities assembled.','Ordering the Past']];
for (const [slug,title,dek,heading] of archiveCollections) { const path=`/archive/${slug}/`; await mkdir(`dist${path}`,{recursive:true}); await writeFile(`dist${path}index.html`,layout({title,description:`Explore the ${title.toLowerCase()} collection in the Tau Gamma Phi digital archive.`,path,crumbs:[{label:'Home',href:'/'},{label:'Archive',href:'/archive/'},{label:title,href:path}],content:`<article class="reader"><p class="kicker">DIGITAL ARCHIVE</p><h1>${esc(title)}</h1><p class="reader-dek">${esc(dek)}</p><section><h2>${esc(heading)}</h2><p>No item is currently published in this collection. That does not mean the history was never created. It means the archive has not yet received material that can be shared here with clear provenance and permission.</p></section><section><h2>Preserving the Record</h2><p>Each future entry should carry its source, date precision, caption, creator or owner where known, and permission to publish. Those details help a reader understand both the item and the history it preserves.</p></section><section><h2>Continue Exploring</h2><p><a class="read-link" href="/archive/">Explore the Digital Archive</a> <a class="read-link" href="/contribute/">Contribute a Historical Record</a> <a class="read-link" href="/corrections/">Submit a Correction</a></p></section></article>`})); }
